# Low Water, Act 3: Lamp Quay in the gale. District file, prefix quay3.
# Beats (design/ACT3-PLAN.md section 3): 1 the quay at sunset, the gale coming, the three gale lamps;
# 7 a boat for the eye (gate B3, five routes, to oldlight.hub); 8 the eye, the town looks up;
# 16 the collier seen from the quay; 18 Keel at high water. Also gate B1's moment for the steps post
# when the town chose it (var light_steps), at the 21:20, 22:40 and 03:30 rain bands.
# Opening node: quay3.start (from day2.dusk).

# ---- new ids
@fact quay3.oil_taken
@fact quay3.post.out
@fact quay3.post.shuttered
@fact quay3.tended
@fact quay3.row.failed
@fact quay3.stowed
@fact quay3.stow_caught
@fact quay3.coffin_sail
@fact quay3.eye_seen
@fact quay3.collier_seen
@fact quay3.keel_seen

@var quay3.boat
default: none
values: none, rowed, merrow, lugg, cockle, stowed, coffin, eye
about: How Lamb went out to the Old Light in the eye. stowed opens the sneak variant of e3.oldlight; eye arrives in the calm, dry, at the eye's first minute.

# ================================================================ BEAT 1: 19:08, SUNSET, THE GALE COMING
@node quay3.start
place: quay
cost: 0
do: set(ev3.dusk)
nar: Eight minutes past seven. The wind has come round the Spit ahead of itself, and every shutter on the quay is up.
inst: THE GLASS: Nine hundred and seventy-one, darling, and dropping. I adore it.
voice: salt: The knees had it at noon. Nobody asks the knees. {dc: 3}
call: quay3.lamps
call: quay3.state
go: quay3.hub

# ---- the three lamps the town chose at the second dawn
@node quay3.lamps
cost: 0
line: COCKLE: Mother's lit for the gale, on the town's oil. {when: var.light_mother == 1}
line: COCKLE: They've lit your post at the top of the steps. It's leaning away from the wind already. {when: var.light_steps == 1}
line: COCKLE: Sabine's porthole's lit behind the shutter. {when: var.light_porthole == 1}
line: COCKLE: The Gut's wires are lit, swinging. {when: var.light_gut == 1}
line: COCKLE: There's a lamp on the town balance, and the balance moving in every gust. {when: var.light_balance == 1}
line: COCKLE: The hill's white lamps are on, cold as you like. {when: var.light_hill == 1}
line: COCKLE: The Old Bulb's glowing in the Gasholder. {when: var.light_bulb == 1}
return:

# ---- who is fallen and who is lit, after two nights
@node quay3.state
cost: 0
line: FEWELL: Fours, still. The book's gone up the hill twice now. {when: has(book.violence)}
line: KEEL: The Board's office is open again, assessor. The Board is open. The Board has nothing in it. {when: has(cause.trust) & has(ink.crake)}
line: COCKLE: Tub's boat's on the steps and Tub's in it, doubling his lines. He says whoever wants the eye can have it. {when: !has(merrow.cells)}
line: COCKLE: Tub's still under the harbour office. Lugg's got his boat on the steps, doubling his lines. {when: has(merrow.cells)}
nar: The broken lens has a tarpaulin over it, lashed down, and the tarpaulin is filling and emptying with the wind like a lung. {when: var.lens == broken}
return:

# ================================================================ THE QUAY IN THE GALE
@node quay3.hub
place: quay
hub: yes
cost: 0
alt: quay3.keel ? clock >= 05:30 & !has(quay3.keel_seen)
alt: quay3.collier ? has(ev3.collier_turn) & !has(quay3.collier_seen)
alt: quay3.eye ? has(ev3.eye) & !has(ev3.eye_ends) & !has(quay3.eye_seen)
alt: quay3.post.dies ? var.light_steps == 1 & clock >= 03:30 & (has(b1.band3) | clock >= 04:10) & !has(quay3.tended) & !has(quay3.post.shuttered) & !has(lampout.steps)
alt: quay3.post.band ? var.light_steps == 1 & !has(quay3.post.out) & !has(quay3.post.shuttered) & ((clock >= 21:20 & clock < 22:00 & !has(b1.band1)) | (clock >= 22:40 & clock < 23:20 & !has(b1.band2)) | (clock >= 03:30 & clock < 04:10 & !has(b1.band3)))
nar: Lamp Quay in the gale, shuttered, with the mole running out into spray.
nar: A rain band comes across the quay sideways, and the sodium lamps go dim and bright as it passes. {when: rain > 0.5}
nar: The wind is from the north-west now. {when: has(ev3.backed) & !has(ev3.surge)}
nar: The sea is over the quay's lip, coming toward the Brine's step. {when: has(ev3.surge)}
opt: "Go along to the mole steps, where the boats are." -> quay3.boats ? !has(ev3.eye_ends) +2
opt: "Get oil and a storm shutter from the harbour office store." -> quay3.oil ? !has(quay3.oil_taken) {verb: carry, noise: 0.1}
opt: "Go into the Brine." -> brine3.hub +1
opt: "Go to the weigh-house." -> weigh3.hub +1
opt: "Walk out along the mole." -> mole3.hub +2
opt: "Go up the lane into the Gut." -> gut3.hub +2
opt: "Climb the hill path in the wind." -> hill3.hub +6
opt: "Go along to the Ropewalk." -> ropewalk3.hub +3

@node quay3.oil
place: harbour
speaker: KEEL
cost: 3
do: set(quay3.oil_taken); give(i.oilcan); give(i.storm_shutter)
line: KEEL: The Board's oil, and a storm shutter off the Board's own lamp. For the town's lamps. Take them. The Board finds, tonight, that it is not sure the difference matters.
go: ^hub

# ================================================================ GATE B1: THE STEPS POST IN A RAIN BAND
@node quay3.post.band
place: steps
speaker: GAUZE
cost: 2
if: clock >= 21:20 & clock < 22:00 => set(b1.band1)
if: clock >= 22:40 & clock < 23:20 => set(b1.band2)
if: clock >= 03:30 => set(b1.band3)
nar: The rain band comes up the steps. In the cage the flame lies flat and blue and does not get up.
line: GAUZE: It's going. Oh, it's going. I can hear it go in here, a little cough.
voice: undertow: Let it. A paraffin lamp on a pole, and you soaked to the ribs for it. Nobody would write it down. {dc: 5}
voice: pride: You would. {dc: 4}
check: "[GRIP] Put your back to the wind at the cage door and trim the wick." -> quay3.post.hold / quay3.post.hold.fail ? count(i.oilcan) >= 1 {skill: grip, dc: 6, verb: light, noise: 0.2, do: take(i.oilcan)}
check: "[CONDOLENCE] Ask Sister Gauze to tend it under her jar, where the wind can't get." -> quay3.post.gauze / quay3.post.gauze.fail {skill: condolence, dc: 6}
check: "[THE DARK] Get down under the cage in the lee of the steps and feed it from below, unseen from the quay." -> quay3.post.lee / quay3.post.lee.fail ? count(i.oilcan) >= 1 {skill: dark, dc: 6, verb: hide, noise: 0, do: take(i.oilcan)}
opt: "Fit the storm shutter to the cage." -> quay3.post.shutter ? count(i.storm_shutter) >= 1 {verb: rig, noise: 0.2, do: take(i.storm_shutter)}
check: "[THE GLASS] Wait for the lull before the next band and fill it then, out of the wind." -> quay3.post.lull / quay3.post.lull.fail {skill: glass, dc: 5, verb: wait, noise: 0}
opt: "Let it go out." -> quay3.post.let

@node quay3.post.hold
place: steps
cost: 4
do: set(quay3.tended)
do: meter(cold, 2)
nar: The wick, trimmed short, takes, and the flame stands up inside the cage and stays.
line: GAUZE: Oh, well done. I heard it come back.
go: ^hub

@node quay3.post.hold.fail
place: steps
cost: 4
do: quest(a3.lamps, lost); set(quay3.post.out); set(lampout.steps); meter(cold, 2); wet(0.3)
nar: The cage door bangs open in a gust and takes the flame with it.
line: GAUZE: There. Gone. It always sounds smaller than you think, going.
go: ^hub

@node quay3.post.gauze
place: steps
speaker: GAUZE
cost: 3
do: set(quay3.tended)
line: GAUZE: In here? Yes. Nothing gets in here. Eleven years and nothing has.
nar: She lifts her jar over the cage, and kneels bareheaded beside the flame in the rain for the first time in eleven years.
go: ^hub

@node quay3.post.gauze.fail
place: steps
speaker: GAUZE
cost: 2
do: quest(a3.lamps, lost); set(quay3.post.out); set(lampout.steps)
line: GAUZE: I can't. I can't take it off. I'm sorry. Ask me something else. Ask me anything else.
go: ^hub

@node quay3.post.lee
place: steps
cost: 4
do: set(quay3.tended)
nar: Under the cage, in the lee of the top step, the oil goes in from below, and nobody on the quay sees who keeps the light.
go: ^hub

@node quay3.post.lee.fail
place: steps
cost: 4
do: quest(a3.lamps, lost); set(quay3.post.out); set(lampout.steps); wet(0.5)
nar: The lee of the step is full of water, and the post goes dark over the assessor's head.
go: ^hub

@node quay3.post.shutter
place: steps
cost: 5
do: set(quay3.post.shuttered); set(quay3.tended)
nar: The flame behind the tin stops dancing and burns like a lamp in a kitchen. It will hold now, whatever comes up the steps.
go: ^hub

@node quay3.post.lull
place: steps
cost: 6
do: set(quay3.tended)
inst: THE GLASS: Now, darling. Forty seconds. Go.
nar: The assessor fills the post in the lull, and the next band arrives on a lit lamp.
go: ^hub

@node quay3.post.lull.fail
place: steps
cost: 6
do: quest(a3.lamps, lost); set(quay3.post.out); set(lampout.steps); wet(0.4)
inst: THE GLASS: Oh. Not that one. The one after. Sorry, darling.
nar: The band arrives on an open cage, and the post goes out under it.
go: ^hub

@node quay3.post.let
place: steps
cost: 1
do: set(quay3.post.out); set(lampout.steps); quest(a3.lamps, lost)
line: GAUZE: Somebody ought to have stayed with it. Somebody always ought.
go: ^hub

# ================================================================ GATE B3: A BOAT FOR THE EYE (before 00:15, or in its first minute)
@node quay3.tiller
place: mole_steps
cost: 2
do: give(w.tiller)
nar: The gale has put a crabber up on the steps on her side, stove in. Her tiller comes out of its socket in one pull, ash, with a rope lanyard still on it.
go: quay3.boats

@node quay3.boats
place: mole_steps
cost: 1
alt: quay3.boats.eye ? has(ev3.eye)
nar: Every boat in the harbour is doubled to the rings and snatching at its lines.
line: MERROW: Eye's at a quarter past. Forty minutes of nothing. Then it all comes back from the other side. {when: !has(merrow.cells)}
line: LUGG: Eye's at a quarter past. Tub would go. {when: has(merrow.cells)}
inst: THE ALMANAC: Low water at twenty-six minutes to one, held up by the surge. The Old Light's base shows from a quarter past midnight to six minutes to one, and not a minute either side.
opt: "Take Merrow's heavy boat and row it out through the last of the gale." -> quay3.row ? !has(quay3.row.failed) {verb: carry, noise: 0.6}
check: "[CONDOLENCE] Ask Merrow to take you out." -> quay3.merrow.ok / quay3.merrow.fail ? !has(merrow.cells) & (rep.lowco >= 1 | has(day2.boats) | has(said.quay2_merrow)) {skill: condolence, dc: 6}
check: "[THE CHIT] Ask Lugg, on what the Shelf said it would do for Merrow." -> quay3.lugg.ok / quay3.lugg.fail ? has(merrow.cells) {skill: chit, dc: 6}
opt: "Ask Nan Cockle for her boat." -> quay3.cockle
check: "[THE DARK] Get into the strippers' boat under the sacks before they go out for the eye." -> quay3.stow.ok / quay3.stow.fail ? !has(quay3.stow_caught) {skill: dark, dc: 6, verb: hide, noise: 0.2}
check: "[GRIP] Rig the Coffin with a scrap sail and a steering oar, for the run home on the north-west wind." -> quay3.coffin.ok / quay3.coffin.fail ? count(i.rope) >= 1 {skill: grip, dc: 6, verb: rig, noise: 0.2}
check: "[THE GLASS] Sit on the steps with the Glass in your hand and go at the eye's first minute." -> quay3.glass.ok / quay3.glass.fail ? clock < 00:15 {skill: glass, dc: 5, verb: wait, noise: 0}
opt: "Pull the tiller out of the wrecked boat on the steps." -> quay3.tiller ? count(w.tiller) == 0 {verb: pry, noise: 0.3}
opt: "Go back along to the quay." -> ^hub +2

# ---- Fist: row through the last of the gale
@node quay3.row
place: mole_steps
cost: 2
check: "[KNEES] Row her out of the harbour mouth against the last of it." -> quay3.row.ok / quay3.row.fail {skill: knees, dc: 7, red}
opt: "Not yet." -> quay3.boats

@node quay3.row.ok
place: eye_water
cost: 25
do: quay3.boat = rowed; quest(a3.eye, boat); quest(a3.eye, out); meter(cold, 3); wet(0.6)
if: clock < 00:15 => wait(00:15 - clock + 1)
nar: Oars and spray, and then oars and spray, holding her off the Spit. Then, between strokes, the wind stops, and the boat sits on flat black water under the stars.
go: oldlight.hub

@node quay3.row.fail
place: mole_steps
cost: 20
do: set(quay3.row.failed); meter(cold, 3); wet(0.8)
nar: The harbour mouth throws the boat back onto the weed of the mole steps.
line: MERROW: Told you. Forty minutes of nothing. You don't row the something. {when: !has(merrow.cells)}
go: quay3.boats

# ---- Tongue: Merrow, Lugg, Cockle
@node quay3.merrow.ok
place: mole_steps
speaker: MERROW
cost: 3
do: quay3.boat = merrow; quest(a3.eye, boat)
line: MERROW: Sit in the middle. We go at the first minute, not before. I'm not rowing the gale for the Shelf.
go: quay3.eyewait

@node quay3.merrow.fail
place: mole_steps
speaker: MERROW
cost: 2
line: MERROW: You've had two nights of my boats. Find your own sea.
go: quay3.boats

@node quay3.lugg.ok
place: mole_steps
speaker: LUGG
cost: 3
do: quay3.boat = lugg; quest(a3.eye, boat)
line: LUGG: You said you'd speak for him. You did, or you will. Either way I heard it. First minute of the eye.
go: quay3.eyewait

@node quay3.lugg.fail
place: mole_steps
speaker: LUGG
cost: 2
line: LUGG: Words don't float, Shelf.
go: quay3.boats

@node quay3.cockle
place: mole_steps
speaker: COCKLE
cost: 2
line: COCKLE: My boat's sound. I'll not take her out at my age. She'll go if you tell her nicely.
check: "[FORM LETTER] Tell her the Shelf will be responsible for the boat." -> quay3.cockle.ok / quay3.cockle.fail {skill: formletter, dc: 5}
opt: "Leave her be." -> quay3.boats

@node quay3.cockle.ok
place: mole_steps
speaker: COCKLE
cost: 2
do: quay3.boat = cockle; quest(a3.eye, boat)
line: COCKLE: The Shelf. Responsible. I'll have that written on the oars.
go: quay3.eyewait

@node quay3.cockle.fail
place: mole_steps
speaker: COCKLE
cost: 1
line: COCKLE: The Shelf's been responsible for a good deal this week, by my count.
go: quay3.boats

# ---- Shadow: under the strippers' sacks
@node quay3.stow.ok
place: mole_steps
cost: 4
do: quay3.boat = stowed; set(quay3.stowed); quest(a3.eye, boat)
nar: Under the sacks it smells of tar and somebody's tea. Boots come aboard, and wait for the calm.
line: SALLIS: First minute of the eye. Bronze gear in the lantern room, and nobody to say whose.
go: quay3.eyewait

@node quay3.stow.fail
place: mole_steps
cost: 3
do: set(quay3.stow_caught); meter(dread, 1)
nar: A hand lifts the sacks and the assessor's face is under the lantern.
line: SALLIS: The Shelf, again. Off. And if we see you out there, we'll know who to thank.
go: quay3.boats

# ---- Hands: the Coffin with a scrap sail
@node quay3.coffin.ok
place: mole_steps
cost: 15
do: quay3.boat = coffin; set(quay3.coffin_sail); quest(a3.eye, boat); take(i.rope)
nar: A spar, a square of the Brine's old awning and an oar over the stern: now she can come home on a north-west wind.
go: quay3.eyewait

@node quay3.coffin.fail
place: mole_steps
cost: 15
do: wet(0.3)
nar: The first gust takes the awning off the spar and away over the mole like a bird with somewhere to be.
go: quay3.boats

# ---- Eye: the eye's first minute, by the Glass
@node quay3.glass.ok
place: mole_steps
cost: 2
do: quay3.boat = eye; quest(a3.eye, boat)
inst: THE GLASS: Watch the needle, darling. When it stops falling, the wind stops. Not before. Not a breath before.
go: quay3.eyewait

@node quay3.glass.fail
place: mole_steps
cost: 10
do: meter(cold, 2); wet(0.5)
inst: THE GLASS: That was a lull, darling. That was not the eye. I did say. I think I said.
go: quay3.boats

# ---- every boat waits for the eye
@node quay3.eyewait
place: mole_steps
cost: 0
alt: quay3.eye.go ? has(ev3.eye)
nar: The assessor sits in the boat at the foot of the mole steps and waits for the needle to stop.
opt: "Wait a little longer." -> quay3.eyewait +5 {verb: wait, noise: 0}
opt: "Wait it out, however long it is." -> quay3.eyewait.long {verb: wait, noise: 0}

@node quay3.eyewait.long
place: mole_steps
cost: 0
if: clock < 00:15 => wait(00:15 - clock + 1)
go: quay3.eyewait

@node quay3.eye.go
place: eye_water
cost: 20
alt: quay3.eye.late ? has(ev3.eye_ends)
do: quest(a3.eye, out)
nar: The wind stops. The oars go into flat black water, and the Old Light's stump comes up out of the dark ahead, wet to its shoulders.
go: oldlight.hub

@node quay3.eye.late
place: mole_steps
cost: 0
nar: The wind comes back from the north-west before the boat is off the steps.
go: ^hub

@node quay3.boats.eye
place: mole_steps
cost: 1
nar: The boats lie still on their lines for the first time tonight.
opt: "Take a boat now, in the calm." -> quay3.eye.go ? !has(ev3.eye_ends) {verb: carry, noise: 0.1, do: quay3.boat = eye; quest(a3.eye, boat)}
opt: "Go back along to the quay." -> ^hub +2

# ================================================================ BEAT 8: THE EYE, 00:15
@node quay3.eye
place: quay
cost: 3
do: set(quay3.eye_seen)
nar: The doors along the quay open one after another, and the town comes out in its nightclothes and stands on the wet stones.
nar: Nobody says anything. A child laughs, and is hushed, and the hush carries the length of the quay.
opt: "Go along to the mole steps while the calm lasts." -> quay3.boats.eye +2
opt: "Stand with them and look up." -> quay3.eye.look

@node quay3.eye.look
place: quay
cost: 5
line: TOBIT: That's all of them. I counted the edge, and that's all of them.
go: ^hub

# ================================================================ BEAT 16: THE COLLIER, 04:00
@node quay3.collier
place: quay
cost: 2
do: set(quay3.collier_seen)
nar: Out in the bay's mouth, a ship's lights: the collier Ellen Varty, coming in on the north-west wind.
voice: sum: Twelve hundred tons, deep laden. A crew of twenty, say. Do not count the crew. {dc: 5}
call: quay3.collier.end
go: ^hub

@node quay3.collier.end
cost: 0
alt: quay3.collier.through ? has(collier.through)
alt: quay3.collier.spit ? has(collier.spit)
nar: Mother's beam goes out across the water and lies on the collier for the length of a breath, and the ship's lights begin, slowly, to turn. {when: mother == burning}
nar: Where Mother's beam should be there is nothing, and the ship's lights come on toward the Spit. {when: mother != burning}
return:

@node quay3.collier.through
cost: 0
nar: The ship's lights find the dog-leg, swing, and come on up the channel between the town's lamps.
return:

@node quay3.collier.spit
cost: 0
nar: The ship's lights stop moving. They stay where they are, out on the Spit, and tilt a little, and stay.
return:

# ================================================================ BEAT 18: KEEL AT HIGH WATER
@node quay3.keel
place: quay
cost: 1
do: set(quay3.keel_seen)
nar: At the quay's edge the harbourmaster stands in the surge to the knee with half the town, and nobody looks at him, because everybody is as wet as he is.
voice: undertow: Ask him now. Tonight he would tell you. {dc: 6}
voice: condolence: Tonight, leave him be. {dc: 4}
go: ^hub

@node quay3.post.dies
place: quay
cost: 1
do: set(lampout.steps); set(quay3.post.out); quest(a3.lamps, lost)
nar: At half past three the band comes up the steps, and the untended post goes out under it.
go: ^hub
